carlos-emr (2026.09.0~snapshot1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian/Ubuntu packaging for a single-VM CARLOS EMR deployment,
    replacing the hand-rolled OSCAR-19-era `dpkg -b` machinery in release/.
    Targets Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (resolute).
  * Ships CARLOS on its own Tomcat 11 CATALINA_BASE running as the
    unprivileged `carlos` system user — never root, never the shared
    distribution `tomcat` user.
  * Front door is nginx + ModSecurity 3 + OWASP CRS in blocking mode,
    HTTPS-only with HSTS, self-signed by default and switchable to a
    certbot-managed Let's Encrypt certificate.
  * MariaDB is provisioned with least-privilege accounts (carlos, drugref,
    backup); the schema is applied with the Flyway migration set shipped on
    the WAR classpath, and the application boots with
    carlos.flyway.onBoot=validate.
  * Nightly restic backups plus a weekly restore drill run as the separate
    unprivileged `carlos-backup` user.
  * Administration is `carlos-ctl` — a Python package mirroring the
    carlos-podman tool's name, language, layout and verb set wherever the two
    deployments share a concept (check, db, db-migrate, db-users, db-dump,
    backup full/verify/status, cert-renew, rotate, status), so operators move
    between the two deployment styles without relearning the tool.
    `carlosctl` remains as a deprecated alias.

 -- CARLOS EMR Maintainers <maintainers@carlos-emr.invalid>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:00:00 +0000
